{
  "_comment": "Soulidity 2-sig fast-path acceptance matrix (11 rows). The harness scripts/smoke-soulidity.ts is a PTB replayer: each step's transactionBase64 must be a real, pre-built PTB encoded as base64. The operator builds these PTBs ahead of time using the SDK builders in web/lib/soulidity/tx/ (e.g. via a one-off Node script that wires builders + smoke wallet keypairs against the testnet/mainnet package id from the deployment manifest), then drops the base64 strings into the placeholders below. The {{txDigest}} token in mirror bodies is substituted at runtime with the digest of the just-signed step. Mirror paths must reference live first-party routes under web/app/api (collection PTB1 mirrors hit /api/collections/create which accepts { txDigest, floorPriceAtomic? }; supply floorPriceAtomic when the collection enforces an off-chain floor). Mirror auth is picked per step.signer: publisher rows use SMOKE_PUBLISHER_*, buyer rows use SMOKE_BUYER_*, agent rows use SMOKE_AGENT_* (see .env.soulidity-smoke.example). Replace every __PLACEHOLDER__ before running. /api/souls/publish and /api/souls/publish/batch mirror bodies use contentSidecars[] entries keyed to emitted ContentVersionAppended events. Each entry shape is { kind, name, versionIndex, sidecar }. Initial mint examples include KIND_SOUL_DOC=0 name \"soul\" versionIndex=0 and KIND_MEMORY=1 name \"default\" versionIndex=0; add KIND_SKILL=2 name \"default\" versionIndex=0 only when the PTB emits an initial skill version. Replace __REPLACE_WITH_*_CONTENT_SIDECAR*__ placeholders with the real Seal envelope sidecars produced by the Walrus upload pipeline, or null for pure-public slots. /api/souls/publish/batch syncBodies entries must be one-per-soul (length === expectedSoulCount); the operator fills each __SOUL_ON_CHAIN_ID_N__ with the actual minted soul id from the same PTB. Standalone skills/assets append rows are PTB-only because current web/app/api has no first-party mirror route for those operations. Plan source: docs/plans/2026-05-03-soulidity-2sigs-fast-path.md sections 7a/7b.",
